vm-8 — Bytecode fasl: serialize compiled functions (plan-2-bytecode-vm).

Turn plan-1's compact fasl into a BYTECODE fasl — the load-speed payoff.

WHAT
- Extend the cfasl object serializer (cfasl-2) with a COMPILED-FUNCTION tag encoding
  { name, lambda-list, code octet-vector, constant pool (recursively serialized;
  may contain nested compiled functions for FLET/LABELS/closures templates),
  arity/&opt/&rest/&key descriptor, max-stack, n-locals }.  Closures' captured cells
  are NOT serialized (they are created at load when the top-level form runs); only
  function TEMPLATES are.
- COMPILE-FILE: after %COMPILE-FILE-TOPLEVEL (compile-time effects) and
  MACROEXPAND-ALL, COMPILE each top-level form (or wrap it so its lambdas compile)
  to bytecode, and serialise the bytecode form via cfasl.  DEFUN/DEFMETHOD bodies
  become compiled functions.  Top-level effectful forms compile to a thunk that is
  called at load.
- LOAD (cfasl-3): deserialize compiled-function objects and install them (no
  re-compilation, no macroexpansion) — this is the big win: ASDF load stops being
  eval-of-trees and becomes install-of-bytecode.
- COMPILE (in-memory): produce a compiled function directly (already the plan for
  the interactive path).
- LOAD-TIME-VALUE: evaluate at load, patch into the constant pool.

ACCEPTANCE: compile a multi-file system to bytecode fasls, load them, and run —
faster load AND faster run than the tree-walker; round-trip a corpus; suite green.
Benchmark ASDF (require :asdf) with bytecode fasls vs the numbers from cfasl-5.

DEPENDS ON: cfasl-1..4 (plan-1), vm-1..6 (compiler emits functions).
